14 Mill Wynd is within the **Glenarrow Town Centre conservation area**. It is not listed, and there is no tree preservation order on the property.

For window replacement, the council's guidance says that replacement windows in a conservation area need a planning application unless they match the existing windows in material and pattern. So:

- If you want to replace the windows with the same material and design as the current ones, you may not need an application.
- If the new windows would differ in material (for example, uPVC instead of timber) or in pattern (for example, a different glazing bar layout or opening style), you will likely need to apply.

I can't give a formal opinion on whether your specific plans need permission. If you tell me the existing and proposed materials and designs, you can check with the council's planning team to confirm before you start work.
